  "findings": "The prior closest composition survives feasibility and is a good test of the strongest smart systems overlap. Consumer Product Design provides fabrication planning, physical mechanisms and prototype tests. Robotics provides kinematics, sensing, force closure and manipulation, and Linear Systems gives feedback, signals and control modelling. Introductory stress and strain, crystallography and sustainable materials support only part of structural mechanics. The second test concentrates energy supply, storage and demand and adds applied water and infrastructure context while retaining life-cycle assessment, partner-facing renewable-system analysis, and physical product prototyping. The first two plans differ by only 15 EC each way and are sensitivity tests of the same foundation. The third plan fixes both unavailable placements, sequences the brain gateway before neurobiology and adds body-system anatomy and its gateway instead of deeper machine learning and geoscience. Computational imaging, sensory-motor science and anatomy provide real points of overlap with medical technology. None develops the linked analysis of structural load, deformation, vibrations and materials that the healthcare precision and instrument project applies. Description-only Perception & Action, Advanced Calculus, Earth’s Resources and Renewable System Design were credited within their documented scope. General computation, renewable-resource assessment and prototypes are genuine contributions but do not supply the required engineering depth and coherence. Academic judgement is based on taught substance, not schedule scarcity or degree-title equivalence. The earlier positive record and reasoning remain traceable in Git."
